# Toolchain: always go through FVM

This repo pins its SDK per-project via `.fvmrc` (currently Flutter 3.47.4 / Dart
3.13.3 — the "Development SDK" row in `PRD.md` §1.5). The system-wide
`flutter`/`dart` on `PATH` can silently resolve to a **different, stale**
version installed via `fvm` globally — bare commands are not trustworthy here.

- Prefer `fvm flutter ...` / `fvm dart ...` over bare `flutter`/`dart`.
- Melos is configured with `sdkPath: .fvm/flutter_sdk` in the root
  `pubspec.yaml`, so `melos` package/workspace operations already use the
  pinned SDK. Still invoke melos itself via `fvm dart run melos ...` to be
  safe.
- To change the pinned version: `fvm use <version>` (updates `.fvmrc` and the
  `.fvm/flutter_sdk` symlink). Never hand-edit `.fvm/flutter_sdk`.
- `.fvm/` (local symlink + cache) is gitignored; only `.fvmrc` is committed.
- The FVM pin is for local dev only. CI must still matrix-test minimum
  (3.38.0) + one intermediate (e.g. 3.44.x) + latest (3.47.4) per `PRD.md`
  §7.2 — do not narrow CI to just the FVM-pinned version.
